Dear Dr. Siam,


thank you for reaching out. It would be great to have you give a talk in ou=
r group to get an understanding if this would be a fit.

While zoom is possible, in person is always better. So if you can travel, I=
 would be happy to sponsor (i.e. pay for) a research visit.


What is the timeline/deadline? I would prefer to do this after CVPR deadlin=
e in two weeks.


Can you say more about the fellowship? What does it cover and how long is i=
t for?


Best, Marcus

________________________________
Von: Mennatullah Siam <mennatul@ualberta.ca>
Gesendet: Samstag, 1. November 2025 15:28:50
An: Rohrbach, Marcus
Betreff: Visiting Assistant Professor

Hello Prof. Marcus Rohrbach,

       I am Mennatullah Siam<https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=3DAV=
Pds3kAAAAJ&hl=3Den&oi=3Dao>, I am leading the Image and Video Understanding=
 lab, previously at Ontario Tech University, Canada, as a tenure-track assi=
stant professor, where I started back in July 2023. I was also an affiliate=
 professor with UBC since 2024. I am sending to inquire about the Humboldt =
fellowship as it has a track for experienced researchers, and I am currentl=
y looking for a short-term visit while I am applying for Faculty positions.=
 I would appreciate your support to help me acquire this fellowship to coll=
aborate with you and your group for a short stay. I can self-nominate for t=
he fellowship, but I need a letter from the German host institution. I thin=
k my research and research goals align well with you and your group.


 My research is focused on Computer Vision, Robotics/embodied AI, Foundatio=
n Models and Responsible AI. I regularly publish in top venues in the field=
, including but not limited to (CVPR/ICCV/TPAMI/IJCV/ICRA/IROS). My current=
 research statement, which outlines my research and future directions, is p=
ublicly available on my homepage, here<https://drive.google.com/file/d/1afw=
Z7MMmcb6jB1hK9us45N5ZB1SQsy1f/view?usp=3Dsharing>. I finished my PhD at the=
 University of Alberta back in 2021 under the supervision of Prof. Martin J=
agersand, and I did my postdoc at York University from 2021-2023. I have ac=
quired funding for my research during my tenure-track appointment, with mor=
e than $300K and previously in my PhD/postdoc positions, I acquired funding=
 and awards up to $220K. I have good recognitions in the field. I was part =
of the team Alberta that won the KUKA innovation finalist award<https://www=
.youtube.com/watch?v=3DaLcw73dt_Oo>. I was also recognized as an outstandin=
g reviewer <https://iccv2023.thecvf.com/outstanding.reviewers-118.php> in I=
CCV'23. I have also given multiple talks, including Black in AI keynote in =
NeurIPS 2022 and founded the Ro'ya-Computer Vision for Africa community tha=
t spurred multiple events, summary is included here<https://x.com/RoyaCV4Af=
rica/status/1807054249777332632>. I also regularly organize workshops in CV=
PR, including the latest PixFoundation workshop<https://sites.google.com/vi=
ew/pixfoundation>, of which I was the primary organizer. I have personally =
also worked on a recent benchmarking effort for the PixFoundation Series<ht=
tps://msiam.github.io/PixFoundationSeries/>, with a benchmarking and an int=
erpretability that focuses on when grounding emerges in pixel-level multimo=
dal large language models<https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.04192> and their video=
<https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.02807> counterparts. I unfortunately had to do =
the work myself because I am hindered in hiring PhD students at UOIT, which=
 is the main reason I am currently looking to relocate to a new position.

I am a female African researcher originally from Egypt, and a Canadian too.=
 I have added my CV<https://msiam.github.io/homepage/docs/CV.pdf> for more =
details. I also have good teaching experience for Discrete Mathematics, Com=
puter Vision and probabilistic machine learning for both undergraduate and =
graduate level courses. I can also contribute to academic service if need b=
e, in addition to the teaching and research duties. I would really apprecia=
te all the support in this transitional phase. If there is an opportunity, =
I can come to TUD as a visiting assistant professor through the Humboldt fe=
llowship or other means you think are more suitable. It is crucial that I d=
on't have gaps in my research experience, and I am currently out of UOIT. S=
uch a research stay can help me bridge this gap and will be a good opportun=
ity to collaborate with you and your group.

Thank you, and I am looking forward to your response.

--
Best Regards,
Mennatullah Siam, PhD, PEng.

